{{Passive skill box|Vaal Pact}}

'''Vaal Pact''' is a [[keystone passive skill]] that grants instant [[life leech]] to [[melee]] attacks, but prevents all other forms of life [[recovery]].

==Mechanics==
Vaal Pact does not affect any other types of leech, such as energy leech or mana leech, as it applies exclusively to life leech. It also has no interactions with {{psl|Ghost Reaver}}.

While only melee attacks gain instant leech from Vaal Pact, life leech from non-melee sources will function normally. By using {{psl|Brutal Fervour}} and a skill that has both a melee and non-melee damage component (e.g. {{il|Molten Strike}}), you can benefit from both instant leech and overleech.

The {{c|mod|Cannot Recover Life other than from Leech}} modifier prevents life recovery from sources that aren't leech or {{il|Temporal Rift}}. This is checked when the player's life is modified; it does not remove life recovery stats from the character entirely. Accordingly, life recovery modifiers can still be used for other purposes through mechanics like {{psl|Zealot's Oath}}, {{psl|Pious Path}}, or {{il|Kaom's Spirit}}. 

Vaal Pact does not affect leech from melee damage dealt by other entities, such as [[minion]]s with {{psl|Bone Barrier}}, or [[Earthbreaker Support|Earthbreaker totem]]s with the {{c|mod|1% of Physical Attack Damage dealt by your Totems is Leeched to you as Life}} [[Totem Mastery]].

==Location==
Vaal Pact is located on the middle layer of the south side, on the east side of the Duelist's area.

